<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahanta people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ahanta are an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> people of the western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankobra-river">Ankobra River</a> and Takoradi. From the 17th century their coast was lined with European trading forts, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> post of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gross-friedrichsburg">Gross Friedrichsburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> forts, and Ahanta rulers signed treaties with the European companies. Their traditional capital is Busua.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahanta-people.jpg" alt="Ahanta people" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghana,_akan,_braccialetto,_oro,_1890-1910_ca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
